  "properties": {
    "title": "Measuring Soil Moisture With GPS Multipath and Open Source Software?",
    "description": "A summary of the GNSS-IR method and a discussion on the deployment of a low-cost, Raspberry Pi-based GNSS-IR system for field-scale soil moisture monitoring.\n\nCan multipath be useful? An emerging measurement technique known as \"GNSS Interferometric Reflectometry\" turns this common source of positioning error into an environmental sensor. \r\n\r\nSee the gnssrefl package by Dr Kristine Larson: https://github.com/kristinemlarson/gnssrefl",
